.TH HTTP_BODY_FLUSH 3
.SH NAME
http_body_flush \- write the queued body of a request
.SH SYNOPSIS
.B #include <http.h>
.P
.BI "ssize_t http_body_flush(http* " h ");"
.SH DESCRIPTION
.BR http_body_flush ()
writes what
.BR http_body (3),
.BR http_chunk (3)
and
.BR http_chunk_end (3)
queued, as far as the socket takes it. It is called by
.BR http_sendreq (3)
and
.BR http_canwrite (3),
there is hardly a reason to call it by hand.
.P
The data goes to the socket directly (through TLS if used), not through the output buffer: the
buffer forgets what a non-blocking socket did not take, the queue of the request does not. When
everything is written the queue is emptied and the socket is not watched for writing any more.
.SH RETURN VALUE
1 if everything is written, 0 if the socket is full (it is watched for writing then) or the headers are not sent yet, -1 on an error with errno set (EPIPE if the peer closed).
.SH SEE ALSO
http_canwrite(3), http_sendreq(3)
